    "excerpt": "CAPILLARIES—Capillaries are tiny (minute) vessels that connect the\nsmallest arteries (called arterioles) to the beginnings of the smallest veins\n(called venules).  Oxygen and other elements are now exchanged for carbon\ndioxide, other gases and metabolic wastes.  These are carried through the\nvenous system back to your ...",
    "fullText": "Your heart is a four-chamber holding and receiving organ with a system of — CAPILLARIES—Capillaries are tiny (minute) vessels that connect the\nsmallest arteries (called arterioles) to the beginnings of the smallest veins\n(called venules).  Oxygen and other elements are now exchanged for carbon\ndioxide, other gases and metabolic wastes.  These are carried through the\nvenous system back to your lungs, kidneys and colon for elimination."
