    "fullText": "There can be many swellings that erupt from the skin during detox. — There can be many swellings that erupt from the skin during detox.  Tumors\ncan even become larger before they are dissolved.  Most swellings are short-\nlived, however, so it is important to keep up the fruit during these times. \nItching is another factor in detoxification.  This is mostly caused by a\nfungal or Candida involvement.  An individual can develop itching and\nredness of the skin anywhere. \nRemedies for Itching During Detoxification\nAngelica Root, Aloe Vera, or Chickweed applied topically can ease the\nitching.  If itching continues, the fungal infestation needs to be killed and the\nlymph they live in must be cleaned.  This requires herbal lymphatic and\nparasite formulas and a raw food diet. \nOTHER SIDE EFFECTS DURING DETOXIFICATION\n \nOther side effects may include, but are not limited to: excessive\nmenstruation; frequent or deep coughing; frequent urination; headaches;\ndiarrhea; numbness; tingling of the arms, legs, hands and feet; skin eruptions\nand gas."
