    "fullText": "Strengthens vascular walls, therefore excellent for regeneration of — Useful for ulcerated conditions. \nHelps remove toxins from the body. \nUseful for prostatitis. \nUse in cases of rheumatism. \nScientific name: Aesculus hippocastanum\nParts used: Bark, dried horse chestnut seeds, dried horse chestnut leaves. \nActions: Anti-inflammatory, anti-rheumatic, astringent, bitter, cellular\nproliferator (especially to the vascular walls), expector ant, febrifuge,\nmild narcotic, nutritive. \nHorsetail or Shavegrass\nHorsetail is one of the greatest herbs for bone and connective tissue\nweaknesses. \nIt is very high in silica, which is converted into calcium by the liver. \nThis herb has great healing powers to all tissues of the body."
