    "excerpt": "These “non-ionizing” bands are\ndivided into two categories: the thermal or heat-producing type, and the non-\nthermal or non-heat producing type.  The thermal or heat-producing currents\nare, of course, the more destructive of the two, to biological tissue. \nWe use non-thermal, non-ionizing energy bands in the medical fi...",
    "fullText": "microwave, radar and infrared currents; and high-level X-rays and gamma — These “non-ionizing” bands are\ndivided into two categories: the thermal or heat-producing type, and the non-\nthermal or non-heat producing type.  The thermal or heat-producing currents\nare, of course, the more destructive of the two, to biological tissue. \nWe use non-thermal, non-ionizing energy bands in the medical field as a\nway of observing and diagnosing tissue weakness.  The EKG and the EEG\ninstruments are two examples of this. \nHumans are coming closer and closer to an understanding of the life\nforce and how it works.  You must always seek truth and remain open\nminded, allowing yourself to grow and explore the endless worlds of God\nwithin and without. \nNOTE — When you are acidic, this condition changes the electromagnetic\nenergy of the body, which causes increased thermal energy and ionization. \nThis damages the tissues throughout your body. \nAROMATHERAPY— USING ESSENTIAL OILS\n \nI’ve always said that if you breathe it, you eat it."
