    "fullText": "pineal gland synthesizes melatonin. — pineal gland synthesizes melatonin.  Melatonin is inhibited when light strikes\nthe retina.  This small gland is considered by many to be the spiritual gland. \nOne of the seats or doorways for Spirit in the physical world. \nPituitary Gland a small, gray, rounded body attached to the base of the brain\nsecreting hormones that regulate the thyroid, adrenals, and other endocrine\norgans.  It is often referred to as the “Master Gland” of the body and secretes a\nnumber of hormones that regulate many bodily processes including growth,\nreproduction and various metabolic activities. \nPlaque a fatty, fibrous, cholesterol-containing mass in the lining of the\narteries and other tissues.  The buildup of plaque in the arteries is a leading\ncause of cardiovascular occlusions, causing strokes and heart attacks.  Plaque\ndeposits on the teeth can lead to gum disease.  Alzheimer’s disease is\nassociated with the accumulation of plaque in the brain tissue causing a lack\nof nutrition to cells."
