    "excerpt": "Trees elevate the groundwater \ntable and draw minerals up into their stems, leaves, flowers and fruits.  This plant \nmatter then eventually falls to the topsoil increasing the mineralization of the soil \nfor more vegetation to grow.  Deciduous trees, which drop their leaves each year, \nstrongly mineralize the topsoil. ...",
    "fullText": "88 | THE SUNFOOD DIET — Trees elevate the groundwater \ntable and draw minerals up into their stems, leaves, flowers and fruits.  This plant \nmatter then eventually falls to the topsoil increasing the mineralization of the soil \nfor more vegetation to grow.  Deciduous trees, which drop their leaves each year, \nstrongly mineralize the topsoil.  \nThe cooking of food is by far the biggest waste of resources on planet Earth.  \nViktoras Kulvinskas, in his classic book Survival Into The 21st Century, \nreports that cooking destroys 85% of the value of food.  When I first realized this, \nUnderstand: you are water - magnetic water.  Everything you swallow must \nbe broken down into a liquid to nourish you.  The tirst thing to go with cooking \nis the water.  \nCooked food is dense.  It leaves a toxic ash, or residue, in the body after it has \nbeen processed as fuel.  Over years and decades, this debris accumulates in the \nform of mucus and is deposited throughout the tissues."
