    "fullText": "90 ] THE SUNFOOD DIET — In third world countries, the cooking of food exposes people to the hazards \nof inhaling wood smoke or emissions from biomass fuels, such as cattle chips \n(dung).  Emissions from wood and biomass fuels are major sources of air pollu-\ntion in the home and are the number one source of air pollution outside the \nhome (even eclipsing fossil fuels).  Studies have shown that cooks inhale more \nsmoke and pollutants than the inhabitants of the dirtiest cities."
