    "excerpt": "Yet, \nwith all the billions of fossils on Earth, no one has met this simple criteria for a \nfossil sequence.  \nWe also do not find any genetic mistakes (one-shot mutations which failed) \nin the fossil record which is impossible if random mutation through natural \nselection (trial and error) is true.  \nBy far the most a...",
    "fullText": "ORICINS — Yet, \nwith all the billions of fossils on Earth, no one has met this simple criteria for a \nfossil sequence.  \nWe also do not find any genetic mistakes (one-shot mutations which failed) \nin the fossil record which is impossible if random mutation through natural \nselection (trial and error) is true.  \nBy far the most abundant fossils in the world are the 14 types of ammonites \n- little shelled snail-like ocean species which, as far as we can tell, have existed \nessentially since life began on Earth.  Literally billions of these fossils have been \nfound, but never have there been discovered any transition types, or smooth \ntransitions, between any of these 14 types.  \nThe first treatise that described that the basic forms of plants and animals did \nnot evolve step-by-step, but were suddenly there, was given by Hugo de Vries \nin his work Mutation Theory in 1886."
