    "fullText": "134 I ORIGINS — For example, the herbivorous cow has been fed the flesh of other \ndead cows, mixed in with its feed, for at least a century by the cattle industry.  \nCows still continue to survive on such food.  Yet, an omnivorist would argue \nthat the cow is no longer an herbivore, but is now an omnivore, because it can \neat something aside from common grass."
