    "fullText": "Here visible in bamboo is the cycloid spiral space curve — It is interesting \nto note that wild chimpanzees, who include animal food in their diet (mostly \ninsects), do not exceed 10% animal food in their nutrition.  \nUnchecked levels of raw animal-food consumption seems to be associated \nwith a poverty consciousness - a subconscious belief that killing, lack and hard-\nship are laws of life.  Repeatedly thinking about demineralized food and \ndeficiency is another facet of a poverty mentality.  Thoughts of lack create lack.  \nThoughts of abundance create abundance.  Feelings of fear along with thoughts \nof lack, deficiency, and doubt lead one to create a reality and diet where those \nthoughts thrive.  \nA few people opt for raw-animal food because they sincerely need nutrients, \nothers opt for this approach due to food addictions and an unwillingness to \ndetoxify.  They want benefits without detoxification, but do not understand that \nsomething for nothing disobeys the karmic law."
