    "excerpt": "152 | ORIGINS \n\"Trust in faith and \nCommon sense \nHave no place \nIn their science. \nThey don't understand \nThe reality they picture \nIs but a reflection — \nOf the thinker. \nDivine and regal, \nIs the grand-ancient world \nThe creation riddle \nCannot be unfurled. \nOut there is a different place, \nOlder, greater, deeper by...",
    "fullText": "152 | ORIGINS — 152 | ORIGINS \n\"Trust in faith and \nCommon sense \nHave no place \nIn their science. \nThey don't understand \nThe reality they picture \nIs but a reflection — \nOf the thinker. \nDivine and regal, \nIs the grand-ancient world \nThe creation riddle \nCannot be unfurled. \nOut there is a different place, \nOlder, greater, deeper by far \nThan the twinkling of \nThe farthest star. \nThe harm to the Earth \nMight be absolved, \nBut her mysteries \nWill never be solved.\" \nORIGINS | 153 \nThey chewed on fruits \nIn the soft, warm breeze. \nAs a waft of smoke \nCaused a monkey to sneeze. \n\"Here they encroach \nOn our Paradise Found \nThey'll slash and burn this \nPlace — to the ground. \nThey don't think \nBeyond the fringe \nOf the tiny world \nThey're living in. \nThey cut then build \nAnother sharp fence, \nWhen all they need is \nWater, leaves... silence. \nMaterialist obsessions, \nThe Survival of the fit \nHas turned the Earth \nInto a fire pit."
