    "excerpt": "758 I DETOXIFICATION \n\"THE CONSTITUTION OF MAN'S BODY HAS NOT CHANCED TO MEET \nTHE NEW CONDITIONS OF HIS ARTIFICIAL ENVI RON M ENT THAT HAS \nREPLACED HIS NATURAL ONE.  THE RESULT IS THAT OF PERPETUAL \nDISCORD BETWEEN MAN AND HIS ENVIRONMENT.  THE EFFECT OF \nTHIS DISCORD IS A GENERAL DETERIORATION OF MAN'S BODY, \nTHE SY...",
    "fullText": "758 I DETOXIFICATION — 758 I DETOXIFICATION \n\"THE CONSTITUTION OF MAN'S BODY HAS NOT CHANCED TO MEET \nTHE NEW CONDITIONS OF HIS ARTIFICIAL ENVI RON M ENT THAT HAS \nREPLACED HIS NATURAL ONE.  THE RESULT IS THAT OF PERPETUAL \nDISCORD BETWEEN MAN AND HIS ENVIRONMENT.  THE EFFECT OF \nTHIS DISCORD IS A GENERAL DETERIORATION OF MAN'S BODY, \nTHE SYMPTOMS OF WHICH ARE TERMED DISEASE. \" \n— Professor Hilton Hotema, Man's Higher Consciousness \n\"LONG-CONTINUED VIOLATION OF THE LAWS OF BEING IS \nTHE CAUSE OF DISEASE; LONG-CONTINUED PERSEVERANCE IN OBEDIENCE IS \nTHE ONLY MEANS BY WHICH HEALTH CAN BE RECOVERED. \" \n— Dr.  Herbert Shelton, Hygienic Review \nThe Physiology Of Detoxification \nIn a world given to superstition, we must always get back to basic simple \nconcepts.  \nOver a lifetime of eating cooked foods, the body gets \"silted up. \" This silt \nconsists of the residues of an improper breakdown of cooked food, the \nelements of which are spread throughout the body."
