    "excerpt": "200 THE SECRET REVEALED \ndigestible.  If not eaten fresh from below the plant or tree, you might consider \nsoaking nuts and seeds in water and/or sprouting them for 3-12 hours to \ndisarm their enzyme inhibitors.  Enzyme inhibitors keep nuts and seeds in their \ndormant state until conditions are right for growth.  If ea...",
    "fullText": "200 THE SECRET REVEALED — 200 THE SECRET REVEALED \ndigestible.  If not eaten fresh from below the plant or tree, you might consider \nsoaking nuts and seeds in water and/or sprouting them for 3-12 hours to \ndisarm their enzyme inhibitors.  Enzyme inhibitors keep nuts and seeds in their \ndormant state until conditions are right for growth.  If eaten in the dormant state \nwithout green leaves to help along digestion, nuts and seeds can burden the \npancreas and sit \"heavy\" in the stomach.  \nIf you eat nuts in moderation and eat nuts with green-leafed vegetables, then \nyou need not worry about soaking or mucus formation.  A strong digestive tract, \nstrengthened by months and years of eating quality high-fiber green vegetables, \nis capable of digesting a small quantity of nuts with little difficulty.  \nSeeds \nMy experience and research has revealed that the best seeds are those \nwhich contain a reasonable ratio of fat to protein."
