    "excerpt": "By \nexperience, I classify them as alkaline fruits.  They are acid in digestion (like \ncitrus fruits), but alkaline in the tissues if broken down properly.  I have found \nthey balance against phosphorus foods, such as avocados and nuts.  \nThe fact that Brook includes animal foods and cooked foods in his chart can \nbe h...",
    "fullText": "A Kirlian image of a radish. — By \nexperience, I classify them as alkaline fruits.  They are acid in digestion (like \ncitrus fruits), but alkaline in the tissues if broken down properly.  I have found \nthey balance against phosphorus foods, such as avocados and nuts.  \nThe fact that Brook includes animal foods and cooked foods in his chart can \nbe helpful to nutritional researchers.  The chart is primarily included to help \npeople make the transition into a raw plant-food regime while feeling balanced \nand healthy.  \nThe philosopher Spencer wrote that perfect correspondence always prevails \nin Nature — one thing is always balanced by another.  You will find by incorpo-\nrating The Sunfood Triangle in conjunction with the CaPNaK Chart that a great \nbalancing occurs and an incredible health arises.  \nNot all foods are listed in the CaPNaK chart."
