    "fullText": "326 I MINERAL TRADE—OUT — This is when the teeth \nproblems arise, which is indicative of the body purging acids and also indicative \nof a lack of minerals in the body and diet, especially calcium, magnesium, iron and \nsilicon.  At the point of mineral trade-out, one needs to take in at least 2. 5 pounds \n(1. 1 kg) of green-leafed vegetables daily (one-third eaten, two-thirds juiced), \nincrease the intake of sea vegetables, use up to ten tablespoons of green super-\nfoods (powdered grasses and algae) per day, include more seeds to help \nsynergize and utilize the green foods and simultaneously cut down on eating \nhybridized sweet fruit and high-fat, acid-forming nuts.  \nmineral.  Interestingly, calcium also makes up about 50% ot the alkaline earth \nmineral matter of the human body, and is found in all bodily tissues, but chiefly \nin the bones, teeth and the muscles.  The importance of leaf minerals for the \nhuman body cannot be overstated."
