    "excerpt": "Meat, raw or cooked, is extremely \nacidic, thus, meat lowers the blood's energy, causing improper mineral precipi-\ntation.  \nSome types of arthritis are definitely linked with an overabundance of cooked, \nacid-forming elements in the body (from meat), and some types are also linked \nto irritants introduced into the bod...",
    "fullText": "326 I MINERAL TRADE—OUT — Meat, raw or cooked, is extremely \nacidic, thus, meat lowers the blood's energy, causing improper mineral precipi-\ntation.  \nSome types of arthritis are definitely linked with an overabundance of cooked, \nacid-forming elements in the body (from meat), and some types are also linked \nto irritants introduced into the body by eating cooked nightshade plants (tomato \nsauce, french fries, baked potatoes, fried eggplant, tobacco, etc. ).  For those with \nan exacerbated arthritic condition I recommend against eating any meat, and to \navoid all nightshades (chilies, eggplants, peppers, potatoes, tobacco, tomatilloes, \ntomatoes), even if eaten raw.  I have noticed with some individuals that sensitiv-\nities to cooked nightshades may continue even when nightshades are eaten \nraw.  \nOsteoporosis also occurs when the blood's acidity is high due to an excess \nof acid-forming foods in the diet.  Remember: the quality of the food entering \nthe body directs the quality of the blood and lymph."
