    "excerpt": "These struc-\ntural dental challenges begin essentially as birth defects and are exacerbated \nby continuous improper nutrition.  T. C.  Fry reported in an article entitled, \"The \nMyth Of Health In America\" which appeared in Dr.  Shelton's Hygienic Review \n(37:7, p.  150-152) that 98. 5% of the US population suffers from...",
    "fullText": "One of the ways anthropologists date human fossils is by looking at skull — These struc-\ntural dental challenges begin essentially as birth defects and are exacerbated \nby continuous improper nutrition.  T. C.  Fry reported in an article entitled, \"The \nMyth Of Health In America\" which appeared in Dr.  Shelton's Hygienic Review \n(37:7, p.  150-152) that 98. 5% of the US population suffers from dental prob-\nlems of one type or another.  These may often be reversed and corrected in one \nor more generations of eating significantly more mineral-rich organic green-\nleafed vegetables, grass (wheatgrass), certain herbs (horsetail tea or bamboo \nsap) and other raw foods in general."
