    "excerpt": "Creative minds may free the Earth, \nWhen action is taken thereon, \nAnd Liberty to those who know: \nWhat you think about — you become.  \nFor thoughts command when people reach, \nOutward towards the stars, \nAnd it was thought which dropped the probe, \nOnto the surface of Mars.  \nIt was thought that ruled, \nWhen the druid...",
    "fullText": "SELECTED POETRY — Creative minds may free the Earth, \nWhen action is taken thereon, \nAnd Liberty to those who know: \nWhat you think about — you become.  \nFor thoughts command when people reach, \nOutward towards the stars, \nAnd it was thought which dropped the probe, \nOnto the surface of Mars.  \nIt was thought that ruled, \nWhen the druids built \nAstronomic Temples of stone and clay.  \nThis is the testimony of the ancients: \nAnd the logic of today.  \nAnd thoughts direct when empires sink, \nIn storms of steel and flame.  \nAnd it is by thought alone \nThat seeds are sown — \nAnd it will always be the same."
