    "fullText": "5f6 | BASIC SUNFOOD WEEKLY MENU — Greek salad containing: lettuce, tomato, cucumber, red onion, salt-cured \nblack olives, 1-2 ounces (30-60 ml) of olive oil.  \n1 item of cooked starch (baked, no-salt corn chips would be preferred) \neaten with one half an avocado.  \n1 sandwich made with toasted sprouted grain bread, avocado, clover \nsprouts, diced red bell pepper, diced tomatoes and diced cucumber).  \nSnacks \n1 bowl of figs or cherries.  \n1 bowl of grapes.  \n1 handful of Brazil nuts.  \nBlended pudding containing: dates, avocado, cinnamon powder, Irish moss \n(a superfood from the sea) and distilled water.  \nOne serving of cooked starch (wholemeal bread, wheat tortillas).  \nDinner \nLarge salad containing 80% green-leafed vegetables, including kale or \nspinach, eaten with 20-30 raw walnuts or macadamia nuts and an orange \nsqueezed as dressing.  \nOne meal of cooked starch (brown rice or baked squash).  \nWarm vegetable soup."
