    "excerpt": "In his \nown words founder Rod Rotondi \nstates: \"Our intention is to create \nhealthful, tasty and affordable foods, \nin their natural state, using only \norganic ingredients, imagination and \nconscious care. \" \nLIVING LIGHT HOUSE \n1457 12th Street \nSanta Monica, CA 90401 \nContacts: Don Kidson \n310-395-6337 \nFax: 310-394-...",
    "fullText": "Angeles restaurant, where anything — In his \nown words founder Rod Rotondi \nstates: \"Our intention is to create \nhealthful, tasty and affordable foods, \nin their natural state, using only \norganic ingredients, imagination and \nconscious care. \" \nLIVING LIGHT HOUSE \n1457 12th Street \nSanta Monica, CA 90401 \nContacts: Don Kidson \n310-395-6337 \nFax: 310-394-2858 \nThe Living Light House hosts \nTuesday and Thursday night raw food \nmeals.  Don invites ecological \nlecturers and activists to present at \nthe house.  \nLYDIA'S LOVIN' FOODS \n31 Bolinas Ave.  \nFairfax, California \n415-456-5300 \nFax: 415-258-9623 \ninfo@lydiasorganics. com \nA beautiful raw-food restaurant \nnestled the paradise of Marin County, \nNorthern, California.  The menu is \ntotally organic and vegan.  Lydia works \nhard to provide you with food filled \nwith love!  Take a trip to Lydia's and \nsupport her and her team's efforts!  \nRAW ENERGY: ORGANIC JUICE CAFE \n2050 Addison (between \nShattuck/Milvia) \nBerkeley, CA \n510-665-9464 \nContact: Vicky Lee \nwww. rawenergy."
