    "excerpt": "44\nRATIONAL FASTING\nthe other way round, for the white corpuscles\nconsist to a large extent of just that famous mucus\ndescribed in such detail during the preceding pages. \nBacteria are being bred outside of the organism on\nmucus rich potatoes, broth, gelatine, etc.  Mucus is\na nitrogenous, vegetable or animal substance...",
    "fullText": "RATIONAL FASTING — 44\nRATIONAL FASTING\nthe other way round, for the white corpuscles\nconsist to a large extent of just that famous mucus\ndescribed in such detail during the preceding pages. \nBacteria are being bred outside of the organism on\nmucus rich potatoes, broth, gelatine, etc.  Mucus is\na nitrogenous, vegetable or animal substance con-\nsisting of an alkaline reacting fluid which contains\ngranulated cells of the same appearance as the\nwhite blood corpuscles.  Perhaps in an entirely\nhealthy\nbody\nthe\nso-called mucus membrane\nshould not be all white and slimy but clean and red\nlike that in animals.  Mucus might even be a chief\ncontributor to wide-spread paleness. \nBy means of this 'mucus theory' we have come to\nexplain away much of the mystery of disease."
