    "excerpt": "Once man is healthy in my sense of the word by\nfasting and following a fruit-diet, that is, free from\nmucus, slime and germ, he, if he stays with the\nfruit-diet, need not fast any longer.  And only then\nwill he find a pleasure in eating which he never\ndreamt of before.  Only in this way will man find\nthe way to happine...",
    "fullText": "REMEDIES — Once man is healthy in my sense of the word by\nfasting and following a fruit-diet, that is, free from\nmucus, slime and germ, he, if he stays with the\nfruit-diet, need not fast any longer.  And only then\nwill he find a pleasure in eating which he never\ndreamt of before.  Only in this way will man find\nthe way to happiness, harmony and the solution of\nall questions, as only through this he can become\nwant-free and get \"nearest to divinity."
