    "excerpt": "Thus all symptoms of aging are latent disease,\naccumulation of mucus and clogging up of the\nsystem with mucus.  Anybody who takes to a\ncareful diet of mucusless foods in case of any\ndisease, possibly followed up by a fast, will rid his\nbody of the dead cells which have accumulated\nthere in the course of many years and ...",
    "fullText": "PRESERVATION OF THE HAIR — Thus all symptoms of aging are latent disease,\naccumulation of mucus and clogging up of the\nsystem with mucus.  Anybody who takes to a\ncareful diet of mucusless foods in case of any\ndisease, possibly followed up by a fast, will rid his\nbody of the dead cells which have accumulated\nthere in the course of many years and will not only\nbetter his condition but at the same time rejuve-\nnate himself.  And whoever rejuvenates himself will\nsimultaneously build up his resistance to disease to\na remarkable degree.  Nobody seems to believe in\nthis possibility.  Yet, each scientific dictionary will\ntell you that under normal circumstances the na-\ntural causes of death should be arteriosclerosis due\nto a slowed down metabolism, i. e. , clogging up of\nthe entire organism, and therefore life ought to end\nwithout any disease whatever."
