    "fullText": "RATIONAL FASTING — 72\nRATIONAL FASTING\ncirculation through the body, especially in the\ntissues, circumvent, dissolve and carry with it the\nmucus and its poisonous substances for eventual\nelimination through the kidneys. \nDuring their fast the primary immediate obstruc-\ntions caused by wrong and too much eating are\neliminated first.  This results in your feeling relative-\nly good, or possibly even better than when eating. \nHowever when--as previously explainedthe blood\nstream begins to carry with it some of the loosened\nmucus matter from the obstructed passages, then\nyou feel miserable.  You and everybody else blame\nthis feeling on the lack of food which is true but\nonly to the extent that this whole cleansing process\nis set into motion by the absence of new food.  The\nnext day for sure you can notice mucus matter in\nthe urine.  Once the waste products have been\neliminated from the circulation you will undoubt-\nedly feel fine, even stronger than ever before."
