    "fullText": "RATIONAL FASTING — 108\nRATIONAL FASTING\nstrict accordance with the condition of the patient,\nbut to combine them as a \"Systematic Cleansing\"\nthe success is remarkable and satisfactory. \nThe great difference between a diet of healing and\na diet of nourishment seems to be almost unknown\nto both practitioners and laymen.  Fruit is the ideal,\npractical and natural diet of mankind, for nourish-\nment, but the Mucusless Diet is a diet of healing\nand consists of raw and cooked fruits, starchless\nand leafy vegetables and mucus poor cereals spe-\ncially prepared.  A special or medical diagnosis is\nnot necessary, nor the local name of the disease,\nbut the amount of encumbrance of mucus and the\nactivity of its toxins is of the first importance, and\nthen, the degree to which the individual's encum-\nbrance has affected his vital energy."
