    "excerpt": "Without stumbling and without losing confidence\nagain, the greatest and most important truth of life\nis revealed to him, the knowledge of the purest,\nbest and most perfect, and at the same time\ncheapest, form of nourishment.  The morbid glut-\ntony disappears by itself, because now he nourishes\nhimself really and rightl...",
    "fullText": "RATIONAL FASTING — Without stumbling and without losing confidence\nagain, the greatest and most important truth of life\nis revealed to him, the knowledge of the purest,\nbest and most perfect, and at the same time\ncheapest, form of nourishment.  The morbid glut-\ntony disappears by itself, because now he nourishes\nhimself really and rightly and does not fill up, to\nsatisfy his enlarged stomach and stimulate it with\nsubstances which, without fail, will lead to disease\nand final death."
