    "fullText": "RATIONAL FASTING — 136\nRATIONAL FASTING\nfunctions.  The anatomy of these micro-organisms\nis known; but the quality of their functions, the\ncauses of their vitality are yet obscure.  They forget\nthat all depends upon the nourishing with live\nblood, and that the fundamental lever of all think-\ningof thinking, itselfhas to be put at the stom-\nach; the center of blood formationif we want to\nsolve the mystery of life.  One has to go to the\ngravity center of the organismthat is, one's stom-\nachin order to understand; alleviate; remedy the\nheaviness; the impediments to one's functions,\nknown as disease.  One has to look into the work-\nings and at the basis of his central organs, if he\nwants to find the cause of accelerated and lowered\nfunctional capacity of all parts of the whole sys-\ntem, which are being nourished with blood, by the\nstomach. \nJean Jacques Rosseau dictated his writings while in\na recumbent position.  Freidrich Von Schiller put\nhis feet into cold water while writing."
