    "fullText": "present among the vegetarian health-seekers “raw food diet” is in fashion. — The secret is simply this: It is a camouflaged fast; the\nstomach and intestines have a rest the same as when fasting, and elimination is promoted\nand the vital organs recuperate.  But when continued longer the bowels constipate from a\nlack of solid food, and it is said that Fletcher himself died thru severe “trouble” in these\norgans. \nAnother camouflaged fast in its effect is the Salisbury cure.  A small piece of beefsteak\nand a little toast, once a day, nothing else.  Relieves, improves, but never heals perfectly. \nUnder the same classification is the milk diet, which puzzles even the most advanced\nexperts of fasting and dietetics by its partial success in many cases."
