    "excerpt": "If you find this difficult to\ndo in the beginning you may drink again later on so that your lunch is taken in the empty\nstomach.  This is so very important that a number of light diseases can be cured by the\nso-called “No BREAKFAST PLAN” alone.  (This subject is more fully covered in Fasting\nLessons 18, 19, 20, 21. )\nI...",
    "fullText": "Transition Diet — If you find this difficult to\ndo in the beginning you may drink again later on so that your lunch is taken in the empty\nstomach.  This is so very important that a number of light diseases can be cured by the\nso-called “No BREAKFAST PLAN” alone.  (This subject is more fully covered in Fasting\nLessons 18, 19, 20, 21. )\nIt is best that no more than two meals a day be eaten, even though the quantity you eat\nis as much as if three or even four meals were eaten.  Later, when the stomach is cleaner,\na small dish of fresh fruits when in season may be eaten for breakfast if desired.  If\npossible, the first meal, lunch, should be eaten between ten and eleven in the morning,\nand supper not sooner than five or six in the afternoon.  Another very important rule,\nwhen eating for health, is SIMPLICITY; in other words do not mix too many kinds of food\nat one meal.  Count the different number of items in the average meal of today and the\ntotal will startle you. \nNEVER DRINK DURING A MEAL."
