    "excerpt": "The bananas would be for a less “mucused” or less acid stomach. \nMenus for the Second Two Weeks\nLUNCH: First a baked apple, apple sauce or other stewed dried fruit.  After ten or fifteen\nminutes a combination salad as suggested in first menu, and bran or whole wheat bread\ntoasted if still hungry.  Cow butter should be ...",
    "fullText": "DRINK THE JUICE ONLY. — The bananas would be for a less “mucused” or less acid stomach. \nMenus for the Second Two Weeks\nLUNCH: First a baked apple, apple sauce or other stewed dried fruit.  After ten or fifteen\nminutes a combination salad as suggested in first menu, and bran or whole wheat bread\ntoasted if still hungry.  Cow butter should be gradually avoided and replaced by a\nvegetable or nut butter during the transition.  By allowing the cooked vegetables to soak\non the salad for 10 to 15 minutes it serves the purpose of a dressing. \nSUPPER: A baked or stewed vegetable as suggested in the first menu, followed with a\nvegetable salad made of lettuce and cucumber or raw celery or a little coleslaw. \nMenus for the Third Two Weeks\nLUNCH: During the summer this should be an exclusive fruit meal-one kind only."
