    "fullText": "Sex (Continued) — The only reasonable change is to\nincrease the eating of natural sweets such as figs, raisins, dates, grapes, etc. \nFeeding the Baby\nIf mother's milk is found to be insufficient or bad, do not use plain cow's milk; it\nshould be diluted with at least one-third to one-half water and sweetened with milk,\nsugar or honey.  Start feeding the baby as soon as possible a teaspoonful of good fruit\njuices (juice from stewed beets is also good), and honey diluted in water between meals. \nThe baby's craving is sweet, and proves that fruit sugar is the “essence” of all dietetics. \nWhat is considered a well-fed and healthy looking baby, of average normal weight, is\nin reality pounds of waste of decayed milk. \nWhether the baby is sick or not, as soon as you commence feeding it fruit juices and\nstewed mash fruits, you will learn from the elimination that I am correct.  The change\nmust therefore be made very carefully.  Babies and children must go thru the same\ncleansing healing process, as do adults."
