    "fullText": "2. Acai ( Euterpe oleracea ) — - Famille Botanique :  - Noms Usuels / Synonymes : Acai - Parties Utilisées : Feuilles, écorce, racines ou plante entière - Catégorie Thérapeutique & Tropisme : Reins & Émonctoires (Drainage Rénal & Lithiases) - Source Primaire Rain-Tree : [Acai Monograph on Rain-Tree.com](https://www.rain-tree.com/acai.htm) - Principes Phytochimiques Actifs :  - The fruit liquid  - 7-11% fats  - 25% sugar  - 05% calcium  - 033% phosphorous  - and 0  - 0009% iron  - It also delivers 88 to 265 calories per 100 grams - Indications & Cibles Thérapeutiques :  - In the Amazon  - the acai palm heart is widely consumed as a vegetable  - In the Brazilian Amazon  - the Indian tribes of the forest use all parts of the tree  - They fell the tree and eat the palm heart  - turn the fruit into a juice drink - Mécanismes & Pharmacodynamie (Leslie Taylor) : 1. Actions Principales (Rain-Tree) : Documenté par Leslie Taylor pour ses principes phytochimiques actifs. 2. Recherche Clinique & Activité Biologique : With acai’s high polyphenol content, it’s not surprising that researchers have studied acai’s antioxidant actions. One of the standard indexes for determining the antioxidant value of various organic compounds is known as the oxygen radical absorbance capacity (ORAC) test. Of all fruits and vegetables—acai berries have one of the highest reported total ORAC scores of any fruit or vegetable. Acai’s... 3. Usage Ethnobotanique Traditionnel : In the Amazon, the acai palm heart is widely consumed as a vegetable, the fruit is prepared into a popular fruit drink and used as a natural ink or dye, and the wood is used in house construction (palm thatched roofs). Ethnobotanists have recorded no less than 22 different uses for all parts of the tree. In the Brazilian Amazon, the Indian tribes o... - Posologie & Modes d'Administration :  - Dosage Standard : fights free radicals relieves pain Fruit juice reduces oxidative stress promotes weight loss As desired reduces inflammation reduces blood pressure protects organs reduces blood sugar prevents clogged arteries reduces anxiety modulates immune system enhances memory slows down aging kills bacteria & viruses protects brain prevents chronic diseases protects bone modulates gut bacteria regenerates bone prevents cancer lowers cholesterol heals wounds  - Infusion / Décoction : 1 cuillère à café à soupe de plante séchée par tasse d'eau chaude, infuser 10-15 min.  - Teinture : 2 à 4 ml (environ 30 à 60 gouttes) 2 fois par jour. - Contre-indications & Précautions :  - None - Note Vitaliste : Fiche botanique officielle Rain-Tree issue des recherches du Dr. Leslie Taylor sur la pharmacopée amazonienne.  ---"
