    "fullText": "4. Achocha ( Cyclanthera pedata ) — - Famille Botanique :  - Noms Usuels / Synonymes : Achocha - Parties Utilisées : Feuilles, écorce, racines ou plante entière - Catégorie Thérapeutique & Tropisme : Reins & Émonctoires (Drainage Rénal & Lithiases) - Source Primaire Rain-Tree : [Achocha Monograph on Rain-Tree.com](https://www.rain-tree.com/caigua.htm) - Principes Phytochimiques Actifs :  - Caigua seeds contain 28-30 amino acids as well as a group of trypsin inhibitors  - Two of these  - chrysin-6-C-fucopyranoside and apigenin-6-C-glucopyranoside (isovitexin)  - were found to be the main constituents in both the leaves and fruits of caigua  - In addition  - the fruits have yielded nine triterpenoid saponins  - among them six new natural compounds never seen before  - The seeds have been reported with six new cucurbitacin glycosides - Indications & Cibles Thérapeutiques :  - In herbal medicine systems in Peru  - The fruits are boiled in milk and gargled for tonsilitis  - The fruit juice is also recommended for high cholesterol  - hypertension  - tonsilitis  - arteriosclerosis - Mécanismes & Pharmacodynamie (Leslie Taylor) : 1. Actions Principales (Rain-Tree) : Documenté par Leslie Taylor pour ses principes phytochimiques actifs. 2. Recherche Clinique & Activité Biologique : Caigua has long been used in traditional medicine systems in South America to balance cholesterol levels. Four early studies and articles published between 1993 and 2003 confirm this traditional use. A human study published in 1995 by Peruvian researchers reported that a dehydrated caigua fruit product reversed the changes in cholesterol experienced by post-menopausal women. They reported that a d... 3. Usage Ethnobotanique Traditionnel : In herbal medicine systems in Peru, a tea from the fruit seeds is used for controlling high blood pressure. The seeds are also dried and crushed and taken in 1-gram doses for intestinal parasites. The seeds and/or the fruits are also recommended for gastrointestinal disorders. The leaves of caigua are considered hypoglycemic and prepared in a decoc... - Posologie & Modes d'Administration :  - Dosage Standard : lowers cholesterol relieves pain Fruit Juice reduces blood pressure reduces inflammation Fresh: 1/4 cup twice daily cleans arteries aids digestion Capsules: 1-2 g twice daily balances blood sugar heals wounds increases urination fights free radicals relieves oxidative stress reduces diabetic complications  - Infusion / Décoction : 1 cuillère à café à soupe de plante séchée par tasse d'eau chaude, infuser 10-15 min.  - Teinture : 2 à 4 ml (environ 30 à 60 gouttes) 2 fois par jour. - Contre-indications & Précautions :  - Consulter un professionnel de santé en cas de grossesse, allaitement ou traitement médical lourd. - Note Vitaliste : Fiche botanique officielle Rain-Tree issue des recherches du Dr. Leslie Taylor sur la pharmacopée amazonienne.  ---"
