    "fullText": "7. Alcachofra ( Cynara scolymus ) — - Famille Botanique :  - Noms Usuels / Synonymes : Alcachofra - Parties Utilisées : Feuilles, écorce, racines ou plante entière - Catégorie Thérapeutique & Tropisme : Reins & Émonctoires (Drainage Rénal & Lithiases) - Source Primaire Rain-Tree : [Alcachofra Monograph on Rain-Tree.com](https://www.rain-tree.com/artichoke.htm) - Principes Phytochimiques Actifs :  - Artichokes are rich in polyphenols  - flavonoids  - anthocyanins  - phenolic compounds  - inulin  - coumarins  - terpenes  - dietary fiber - Indications & Cibles Thérapeutiques :  - In Brazilian herbal medicine systems  - diabetes  - high cholesterol  - hypertension  - anemia  - diarrhea (and elimination in general) - Mécanismes & Pharmacodynamie (Leslie Taylor) : 1. Actions Principales (Rain-Tree) : Documenté par Leslie Taylor pour ses principes phytochimiques actifs. 2. Recherche Clinique & Activité Biologique : Investigations are still being conducted on artichoke's beneficial effects on liver and gallbladder functions. In 2002, researchers noted that an artichoke leaf extract reversed damage done by harmful chemicals in rat liver cells and, in doing so, enhanced bile production. Many other studies followed recording several ways that artichoke can help to protect the liver from various conditions and ch... 3. Usage Ethnobotanique Traditionnel : Artichoke has been used in traditional medicine for centuries as a specific liver and gallbladder remedy. In Brazilian herbal medicine systems, leaf preparations are used for liver and gallbladder problems, diabetes, high cholesterol, hypertension, anemia, diarrhea (and elimination in general), fevers, ulcers, and gout. In Europe, it is also used f... - Posologie & Modes d'Administration :  - Dosage Standard : reduces cholesterol kills cancer cells Leaves or fruit lowers blood pressure slows aging Infusion: 1-3 cups daily stimulates bile cleanses blood Liquid extract: 2-3 ml with supports & protects liver increases urination each meal protects brain & heart detoxifies Capsules: 2-3 g 3 times daily enhances digestion kills bacteria and fungi Standardized Extracts: fights free radicals supports gallbladder function follow label directions relieves oxidative stress relieves digestive disorders protects organs slows aging reduces inflammation prevents metabolic syndrome modulates immune system relieves pain balances blood glucose prevents chronic diseases  - Infusion / Décoction : 1 cuillère à café à soupe de plante séchée par tasse d'eau chaude, infuser 10-15 min.  - Teinture : 2 à 4 ml (environ 30 à 60 gouttes) 2 fois par jour. - Contre-indications & Précautions :  - Consulter un professionnel de santé en cas de grossesse, allaitement ou traitement médical lourd. - Note Vitaliste : Fiche botanique officielle Rain-Tree issue des recherches du Dr. Leslie Taylor sur la pharmacopée amazonienne.  ---"
