    "fullText": "11. Andiroba ( Carapa guianensis ) — - Famille Botanique : Plante Amazonienne - Noms Usuels / Synonymes : Andiroba - Parties Utilisées : Feuilles, écorce, racines ou plante entière - Catégorie Thérapeutique & Tropisme : Foie & Digestion (Hépato-Biliaire & Détox) - Source Primaire Rain-Tree : [Andiroba Monograph on Rain-Tree.com](https://www.rain-tree.com/andiroba.htm) - Principes Phytochimiques Actifs :  - Andiroba oil is a rich source of essential fatty acids including oleic  - palmitic  - stearic  - and linoleic acids with a predominance of oleic acid (47  - 62%)  - Oleic acid performs various actions  - including regulating blood lipids  - reducing inflammation - Indications & Cibles Thérapeutiques :  - and virtually all parts of the tree  - as well as the seed oil are utilized  - The Wayapi  - Palikur  - for other skin parasites  - and even in the process of tanning animal hides - Mécanismes & Pharmacodynamie (Leslie Taylor) : 1. Actions Principales (Rain-Tree) : Documenté par Leslie Taylor pour ses principes phytochimiques actifs. 2. Recherche Clinique & Activité Biologique : Andiroba oil has demonstrated broad spectrum pharmacological activities in clinical research. The oil extracted from its seeds has antimicrobial effects against Staphylococcus aureus, Escherichia coli and Candida albicans. Its bioactive compounds, such as limonoids and fatty acids, have demonstrated anti-inflammatory properties, speeding up wound healing and relieving pain, particularly in cases s... 3. Usage Ethnobotanique Traditionnel : The indigenous peoples in the Amazon have used andiroba in many ways for centuries, and virtually all parts of the tree, as well as the seed oil are utilized. The Munduruku Indians traditionally used the oil for the mummification of human heads taken as war trophies. The Wayapi, Palikur, and Creole Indian tribes have used andiroba oil to remove tic... - Posologie & Modes d'Administration :  - Dosage Standard : heals wounds soothes skin Seed Oil reduces pain reduces fever External: Applied topically to reduces inflammation prevents cancer skin as needed. kills bacteria kills cancer cells Internal: 2 ml 2-3 times daily relaxes muscles kills insects kills parasites expels worms fights free radicals relieves oxidative stress relieves allergies repels insects  - Infusion / Décoction : 1 cuillère à café à soupe de plante séchée par tasse d'eau chaude, infuser 10-15 min.  - Teinture : 2 à 4 ml (environ 30 à 60 gouttes) 2 fois par jour. - Contre-indications & Précautions :  - None reported. - Note Vitaliste : Fiche botanique officielle Rain-Tree issue des recherches du Dr. Leslie Taylor sur la pharmacopée amazonienne.  ---"
