    "fullText": "20. Brazilian Peppertree ( Schinus molle ) — - Famille Botanique :  - Noms Usuels / Synonymes : Brazilian Peppertree - Parties Utilisées : Feuilles, écorce, racines ou plante entière - Catégorie Thérapeutique & Tropisme : Reins & Émonctoires (Drainage Rénal & Lithiases) - Source Primaire Rain-Tree : [Brazilian Peppertree Monograph on Rain-Tree.com](https://www.rain-tree.com/peppertree.htm) - Principes Phytochimiques Actifs :  - alkaloids  - flavonoids  - steroidal saponins  - sterols  - terpenes  - triterpenoids  - The essential oil present in the leaves  - bark - Indications & Cibles Thérapeutiques :  - Virtually all parts of this tropical tree  - including its leaves  - bark  - fruit  - seeds  - resin - Mécanismes & Pharmacodynamie (Leslie Taylor) : 1. Actions Principales (Rain-Tree) : Documenté par Leslie Taylor pour ses principes phytochimiques actifs. 2. Recherche Clinique & Activité Biologique : The first area of extensive research on Brazilian peppertree (includes 3 human studies and numerous animal and in vitro studies) have confirmed that all parts of the tree provide potent antimicrobial actions against a wide variety of pathogenic bacteria, mycobacteria and mycoplasma, viruses, yeasts, mold and fungi that plague humans, animals and livestock, as well as plants and crops. Numerous nat... 3. Usage Ethnobotanique Traditionnel : Virtually all parts of this tropical tree, including its leaves, bark, fruit, seeds, resin, and oleoresin (or balsam) have been used medicinally by indigenous peoples throughout the tropics for centuries. The plant has a very long history of use and appears in ancient religious artifacts and on idols among some of the ancient Chilean Amerindians. W... - Posologie & Modes d'Administration :  - Dosage Standard : kills bacteria and viruses relieves depression Leaf, Bark, Fruit kills fungi and Candida kills cancer cells Bark Decoction: 1/2 cup relieves pain stimulates digestion twice daily reduces inflammation reduces spasms Leaf Infusion: 1/2 cup heals wounds kills parasites twice daily regulates heartbeat kills insects Tincture: 2-3 ml twice daily lowers blood pressure increases urination fights free radicals modulates immune response relieves oxidative stress reduces phlegm protect organs prevents diabetic complications prevents chronic diseases promotes healthy aging promotes healthy cholesterol balances blood sugar  - Infusion / Décoction : 1 cuillère à café à soupe de plante séchée par tasse d'eau chaude, infuser 10-15 min.  - Teinture : 2 à 4 ml (environ 30 à 60 gouttes) 2 fois par jour. - Contre-indications & Précautions :  - Consulter un professionnel de santé en cas de grossesse, allaitement ou traitement médical lourd. - Note Vitaliste : Fiche botanique officielle Rain-Tree issue des recherches du Dr. Leslie Taylor sur la pharmacopée amazonienne.  ---"
