    "fullText": "26. Camu-Camu ( Myrciaria dubia ) — - Famille Botanique :  - Noms Usuels / Synonymes : Camu-Camu - Parties Utilisées : Feuilles, écorce, racines ou plante entière - Catégorie Thérapeutique & Tropisme : Reins & Émonctoires (Drainage Rénal & Lithiases) - Source Primaire Rain-Tree : [Camu-Camu Monograph on Rain-Tree.com](https://www.rain-tree.com/camu.htm) - Principes Phytochimiques Actifs :  - Oranges provide 500 to 4  - 000 ppm (parts per million) vitamin C  - or ascorbic acid  - acerola  - another tropical fruit featured in this book  - has tested in the range of 16  - 000 to 172  - 000 ppm - Indications & Cibles Thérapeutiques :  - In fact  - acidic taste  - However  - parasitic infections  - and other medicinal purposes for hundreds of years  - Today - Mécanismes & Pharmacodynamie (Leslie Taylor) : 1. Actions Principales (Rain-Tree) : Documenté par Leslie Taylor pour ses principes phytochimiques actifs. 2. Recherche Clinique & Activité Biologique : The first study on camu-camu’s polyphenol antioxidants was published in 2005 when two anthocyanin chemicals were discovered. Between 2007 and 2013 four more studies were published reporting new antioxidant chemicals in the fruit and measuring their actions. In 2008 a research group performed a human study on camu-camu’s antioxidant and anti-inflammatory actions. Twenty habitual male smokers who we... 3. Usage Ethnobotanique Traditionnel : Camu camu fruit was never documented as a traditional herbal remedy for any condition in the Amazon region before a market was created for it in the United States and Japan. In fact, it wasn’t even widely eaten as a fruit by the indigenous people due to its sour, acidic taste. However, the leaves and bark of the camu camu shrub have been used by ra... - Posologie & Modes d'Administration :  - Dosage Standard : is nutritious balances cholesterol Fruit fights free radicals prevents cancer Fresh Juice: 1 cup 2-3 times daily relieves oxidative stress kills cancer cells Capsules: 1-2 g twice daily or protects cells & organs lowers blood sugar follow label directions based on promotes weight loss lowers blood pressure Vitamin C content kills bacteria enhances fertility slows aging relieves inflammation prevents chronic diseases  - Infusion / Décoction : 1 cuillère à café à soupe de plante séchée par tasse d'eau chaude, infuser 10-15 min.  - Teinture : 2 à 4 ml (environ 30 à 60 gouttes) 2 fois par jour. - Contre-indications & Précautions :  - None reported. Side effects for high or excessive dosages of vitamin C include gastrointestinal disturbances and diarrhea. - Note Vitaliste : Fiche botanique officielle Rain-Tree issue des recherches du Dr. Leslie Taylor sur la pharmacopée amazonienne.  ---"
