    "fullText": "28. Canchalagua ( Schkuhria pinnata ) — - Famille Botanique :  - Noms Usuels / Synonymes : Canchalagua - Parties Utilisées : Feuilles, écorce, racines ou plante entière - Catégorie Thérapeutique & Tropisme : Reins & Émonctoires (Drainage Rénal & Lithiases) - Source Primaire Rain-Tree : [Canchalagua Monograph on Rain-Tree.com](https://www.rain-tree.com/canchalagua.htm) - Principes Phytochimiques Actifs :  - Canchalagua contains germacranolides  - heliangolides  - sesquiterpene lactones  - flavonoids  - and sulfur compounds  - In general  - these polyphenols provide effective antioxidant  - anti-inflammatory and antimicrobial actions - Indications & Cibles Thérapeutiques :  - Many types of skin problems  - including eczema  - dermatitis  - and acne  - digestive  - antitussive (stops coughing) - Mécanismes & Pharmacodynamie (Leslie Taylor) : 1. Actions Principales (Rain-Tree) : Documenté par Leslie Taylor pour ses principes phytochimiques actifs. 2. Recherche Clinique & Activité Biologique : Canchalagua's traditional use as an antimicrobial remedy against various infections has been validated thru various studies. It was shown to be active against several fungus, yeast and mold strains and using the entire plant rather than just the leaves yielded much better activity. Its actions against bacteria has been mixed, but in the tests reported, they were mostly working with just leaves and... 3. Usage Ethnobotanique Traditionnel : Canchalagua is the Peruvian name given to this plant by the Ketchwa indigenous people of the Andes. They have long used this plant as an effective blood cleanser. Usually the entire plant is uprooted and chopped up and brewed into an infusion (fresh plant) or a decoction (dried plant) for this local remedy. Many types of skin problems, including ec... - Posologie & Modes d'Administration :  - Dosage Standard : cleanses blood heals wounds Aerial parts reduces acne eases nausea Infusion: 1 cup 3 times daily aids digestion kills mold & fungi Capsules: 1-2 g twice daily fights free radicals relieves pain reduces inflammation lowers blood sugar increases urination kills cancer cells reduces spasms cleanses liver & kidneys kills bacteria kills parasites  - Infusion / Décoction : 1 cuillère à café à soupe de plante séchée par tasse d'eau chaude, infuser 10-15 min.  - Teinture : 2 à 4 ml (environ 30 à 60 gouttes) 2 fois par jour. - Contre-indications & Précautions :  - None reported. - Note Vitaliste : Fiche botanique officielle Rain-Tree issue des recherches du Dr. Leslie Taylor sur la pharmacopée amazonienne.  ---"
