    "fullText": "34. Catuaba ( Erythroxylum catuaba ) — - Famille Botanique :  - Noms Usuels / Synonymes : Catuaba - Parties Utilisées : Feuilles, écorce, racines ou plante entière - Catégorie Thérapeutique & Tropisme : Reins & Émonctoires (Drainage Rénal & Lithiases) - Source Primaire Rain-Tree : [Catuaba Monograph on Rain-Tree.com](https://www.rain-tree.com/catuaba.htm) - Principes Phytochimiques Actifs :  - The chemical constituents found in catuaba include alkaloids  - tannins  - aromatic oils and fatty resins  - phytosterols  - cyclolignans  - sequiterpenes  - and flavonoids  - The polyphenols in catuaba have demonstrated antioxidant - Indications & Cibles Thérapeutiques :  - It is the most famous of all Brazilian aphrodisiac plants  - In the Brazilian state of Minas there is a saying  - \"Until a father reaches 60  - the son is his  - after that  - the son is catuaba's!\" In Brazilian herbal medicine today - Mécanismes & Pharmacodynamie (Leslie Taylor) : 1. Actions Principales (Rain-Tree) : Documenté par Leslie Taylor pour ses principes phytochimiques actifs. 2. Recherche Clinique & Activité Biologique : Only one study has been conducted on catuaba’s ability to enhance erectile function. It was published in 2001 using a standard model of animal research used to determine if a substance can enhance erectile function in rabbits by facilitating blood flow to the penis. Catuaba passed this test, and compared to several other Brazilian plants used as aphrodisiacs, it was the only plant which provided a... 3. Usage Ethnobotanique Traditionnel : Catuaba has a long history of use in herbal medicine as an aphrodisiac. The Tupi Indians in Brazil first discovered the aphrodisiac qualities of the plant and over the last few centuries they have composed many songs praising its wonders and abilities. Indigenous and local peoples have used catuaba for generations. It is the most famous of all Braz... - Posologie & Modes d'Administration :  - Dosage Standard : increases libido relieves pain Bark calms nerves kills bacteria Infusion: 1 cup 1-3 times daily reduces anxiety kills viruses Tincture: 2-3 ml twice daily relieves depression dilates blood vessels kills candida & fungi relaxes blood vessels fights free radicals protects organs enhances memory kills cancer cells reduces inflammation reduces oxidative stress relaxes muscles increases erectile function protects and heals brain  - Infusion / Décoction : 1 cuillère à café à soupe de plante séchée par tasse d'eau chaude, infuser 10-15 min.  - Teinture : 2 à 4 ml (environ 30 à 60 gouttes) 2 fois par jour. - Contre-indications & Précautions :  - Consulter un professionnel de santé en cas de grossesse, allaitement ou traitement médical lourd. - Note Vitaliste : Fiche botanique officielle Rain-Tree issue des recherches du Dr. Leslie Taylor sur la pharmacopée amazonienne.  ---"
