    "fullText": "36. Ch&aacute; de Bugre ( Cordia salicifolia ) — - Famille Botanique :  - Noms Usuels / Synonymes : Ch&aacute; de Bugre - Parties Utilisées : Feuilles, écorce, racines ou plante entière - Catégorie Thérapeutique & Tropisme : Reins & Émonctoires (Drainage Rénal & Lithiases) - Source Primaire Rain-Tree : [Ch&aacute; de Bugre Monograph on Rain-Tree.com](https://www.rain-tree.com/chadebugre.htm) - Principes Phytochimiques Actifs :  - At present it is known to contain caffeine  - potassium  - allantoin and allantoic acid  - Main plant chemicals include (+)-spathulenol  - allantoin  - allantoic acid  - caffeine  - and potassium - Indications & Cibles Thérapeutiques :  - stores  - appetite suppressant  - Several years ago  - Cruz in his book  - Dictionary of the Plants Used in Brazil  - regulate renal function - Mécanismes & Pharmacodynamie (Leslie Taylor) : 1. Actions Principales (Rain-Tree) : Documenté par Leslie Taylor pour ses principes phytochimiques actifs. 2. Recherche Clinique & Activité Biologique : Since cha de bugre is a commonly sold and a popular natural product already, very little clinical research or interest has been shown to study the plant in Brazil. However, Brazilian researchers published an animal study (with rats) in 2022 which confirmed the anti-obesity actions of cha de bugre. They reported that when they gave diet-induced obese rats cha de bugre (at a dosage of 500 mg per kg ... 3. Usage Ethnobotanique Traditionnel : Cha de bugre products are highly commercialized as a weight loss aid in Brazil where tea bags, fluid extracts and tinctures of cha de bugre are commonly seen in pharmacies, stores, and even in the beach-front eateries and refreshment stands along Rio de Janeiro's beaches (where bikinis rule!). It has long been a popular weight loss product which ha... - Posologie & Modes d'Administration :  - Dosage Standard : decreases appetite kills viruses Leaves reduces cellulite reduces fever Infusion: 1 cup 1/2 to promotes weight loss neutralizes venom 1 hour before meals supports heart function Tincture: 2-3 ml 2-3 times daily stimulates Capsules: 2-3 g twice daily increases urination reduces triglycerides  - Infusion / Décoction : 1 cuillère à café à soupe de plante séchée par tasse d'eau chaude, infuser 10-15 min.  - Teinture : 2 à 4 ml (environ 30 à 60 gouttes) 2 fois par jour. - Contre-indications & Précautions :  - None reported. - Note Vitaliste : Fiche botanique officielle Rain-Tree issue des recherches du Dr. Leslie Taylor sur la pharmacopée amazonienne.  ---"
