    "excerpt": "- Famille Botanique : Asteraceae - Noms Usuels / Synonymes : Cipo Cabeludo - Parties Utilisées : Feuilles, écorce, racines ou plante entière - Catégorie Thérapeutique & Tropisme : Reins & Émonctoires (Drainage Rénal & Lithiases) - Source Primaire Rain-Tree : [Cipo Cabeludo Monograph on Rain-Tree.com](https://www.rain-t...",
    "fullText": "39. Cipo Cabeludo ( Mikania hirsutissima ) — - Famille Botanique : Asteraceae - Noms Usuels / Synonymes : Cipo Cabeludo - Parties Utilisées : Feuilles, écorce, racines ou plante entière - Catégorie Thérapeutique & Tropisme : Reins & Émonctoires (Drainage Rénal & Lithiases) - Source Primaire Rain-Tree : [Cipo Cabeludo Monograph on Rain-Tree.com](https://www.rain-tree.com/cipocabeludo.htm) - Principes Phytochimiques Actifs :  - Chemical screening has revealed that cipo cabeludo contains coumarin  - sesquiterpenes  - flavonols  - saponins  - and kaurenoic acid derivatives  - These acid derivatives are chemicals that have been documented with various - Indications & Cibles Thérapeutiques :  - Cipo cabeludo is used in herbal medicine as a diuretic  - While these effects have not been confirmed scientifically  - therefore  - it is probably best to avoid chronic use of this plant  - While not substantiated scientifically - Mécanismes & Pharmacodynamie (Leslie Taylor) : 1. Actions Principales (Rain-Tree) : 1. Cipo cabeludo is used in herbal medicine as a diuretic. While these effects have not been confirmed scientifically, use of this plant may be contraindicated in various medical conditions where diuretics are not appropriate. Chronic long-term use of any diuretic can cause electrolyte and mineral imbalances as well as other medical problems and are generally not recommended; therefore, it is probably best to avoid chronic use of this plant. 2. While not substantiated scientifically, it is possible that cipo cabeludo may demonstrate a blood thinning effect due to its coumarin content. Consult your doctor before using this plant if you are taking coumadin drugs (or if coumadin anticoagulant-type drugs are contraindicated for your condition). 2. Recherche Clinique & Activité Biologique : This particular species of Mikania was described by a Brazilian researcher at the University of Sao Paulo in the early 1970s. In the mid-eighties, other Brazilian researchers documented that an extract of cipo cabeludo had powerful molluscicidal effects (it had a lethal effect against adult snails) at only 10 ppm concentration. This type of test generally is conducted on plants in the ongoing sear... 3. Usage Ethnobotanique Traditionnel : Cipo cabeludo is widely used in Brazilian herbal medicine and highly regarded as a powerful diuretic. Its main documented uses there are for cystitis, prostatitis, urethritis, gout, urinary tract infections, excessive mucus, gallstones, kidney stones, and to help lower uric acid levels in the urine and blood. It is a preferred natural remedy for ne... - Posologie & Modes d'Administration :  - Dosage Standard : relieves pain kills leukemia cells Vine, Leaves reduces inflammation kills cancer cells Infusion: 1/2 cup twice daily increases urination calms nerves Tincture: 5-10 ml twice daily thins blood reduces mucus fights free radicals protects cells & organs kills bacteria improves kidney function improves prostate function  - Infusion / Décoction : 1 cuillère à café à soupe de plante séchée par tasse d'eau chaude, infuser 10-15 min.  - Teinture : 2 à 4 ml (environ 30 à 60 gouttes) 2 fois par jour. - Contre-indications & Précautions :  - 1. Cipo cabeludo is used in herbal medicine as a diuretic. While these effects have not been confirmed scientifically, use of this plant may be contraindicated in various medical conditions where diuretics are not appropriate. Chronic long-term use of any diuretic can cause electrolyte and mineral imbalances as well as other medical problems and are generally not recommended; therefore, it is probably best to avoid chronic use of this plant. 2. While not substantiated scientifically, it is possible that cipo cabeludo may demonstrate a blood thinning effect due to its coumarin content. Consult your doctor before using this plant if you are taking coumadin drugs (or if coumadin anticoagulant-type drugs are contraindicated for your condition). - Note Vitaliste : Fiche botanique officielle Rain-Tree issue des recherches du Dr. Leslie Taylor sur la pharmacopée amazonienne.  ---"
