    "fullText": "47. Cumanda ( Campsiandra laurifolia ) — - Famille Botanique : Fabaceae or Caesalpiniaceae - Noms Usuels / Synonymes : huacapurana, acapurana, acapu-do-igapo, apikara, caacapoc, cumand&aacute, gapo - Parties Utilisées : Bark - Catégorie Thérapeutique & Tropisme : Antiparasitaire & Antifongique (Purification & Antiparasitaire) - Source Primaire Rain-Tree : [Cumanda Monograph on Rain-Tree.com](https://www.rain-tree.com/campsiandra.htm) - Principes Phytochimiques Actifs :  - The chemicals in huacapurana bark have not been fully studied or reported  - It is believed to contain anthocyanins  - cyanogenic glucosides  - heterosides  - saponins  - and tannins - Indications & Cibles Thérapeutiques :  - In the Iquitos region  - In herbal medicine systems in Peru  - diarrhea  - as a tonic  - and for other feverish conditions  - The Witoto Indians in the area use the pulverized bark of C - Mécanismes & Pharmacodynamie (Leslie Taylor) : 1. Actions Principales (Rain-Tree) : Documenté par Leslie Taylor pour ses principes phytochimiques actifs. 2. Recherche Clinique & Activité Biologique : There have been no laboratory studies or clinical research published on huacapurana bark in any peer-reviewed journals or publications. A university in Ecuador was paid to run several studies on a U.S. manufactured huacapurana extract by the company marketing this extract. To date, these studies have not been published in any independent journal or subjected to peer review. Current Practical Uses ... 3. Usage Ethnobotanique Traditionnel : Huacapurana (all three species) is a common remedy for malarial fever in Peruvian Amazon. In the Iquitos region, local herbalists and curanderos recommend a decoction or a tincture of the bark to be taken twice daily to reduce the fever related to malaria. In herbal medicine systems in Peru, huacapurana is also recommended for arthritis and rheumat... - Posologie & Modes d'Administration :  - Dosage Standard : febrifuge anti-ulcer Bark tonic Tincture or Decoction antiarthritic vulnerary  - Infusion / Décoction : 1 cuillère à café à soupe de plante séchée par tasse d'eau chaude, infuser 10-15 min.  - Teinture : 2 à 4 ml (environ 30 à 60 gouttes) 2 fois par jour. - Contre-indications & Précautions :  - None known. - Note Vitaliste : Fiche botanique officielle Rain-Tree issue des recherches du Dr. Leslie Taylor sur la pharmacopée amazonienne.  ---"
