    "fullText": "56. Espinheira Santa ( Maytenus ilicifolia ) — - Famille Botanique : Plante Amazonienne - Noms Usuels / Synonymes : Espinheira Santa - Parties Utilisées : Feuilles, écorce, racines ou plante entière - Catégorie Thérapeutique & Tropisme : Reins & Émonctoires (Drainage Rénal & Lithiases) - Source Primaire Rain-Tree : [Espinheira Santa Monograph on Rain-Tree.com](https://www.rain-tree.com/espinheira.htm) - Principes Phytochimiques Actifs :  - In the 1990s  - squamous cell carcinoma  - and renal cell carcinoma  - Other important triterpene chemicals occurring in the plant include pristimerin  - celastrol  - Following the 1970’s NCI research  - maytansine and mayteine (alkaloids)  - further research was not continued due to the toxicity at the dosages used - Indications & Cibles Thérapeutiques :  - It has been used by some native groups in Paraguay  - and to induce menstruation and abortions  - probably because of the types of illnesses that it treats  - In Brazil  - indigestion  - chronic gastritis - Mécanismes & Pharmacodynamie (Leslie Taylor) : 1. Actions Principales (Rain-Tree) : Documenté par Leslie Taylor pour ses principes phytochimiques actifs. 2. Recherche Clinique & Activité Biologique : Espinheira santa has been the subject of many clinical studies, fueled by its effectiveness in treating ulcers and even cancer, with research beginning as early as the mid-1960s. Early research performed in Brazil in the early 1970s revealed that espinheira santa, as well as a few other species in the Maytenus family, contains maytansinoid chemical compounds that showed potent antitumor and antile... 3. Usage Ethnobotanique Traditionnel : This particular Maytenus species has not been used as extensively by the indigenous peoples in the Amazon region as other Maytenus trees in the area. It has been used by some native groups in Paraguay, where women use the plant as a contraceptive and fertility regulator, and to induce menstruation and abortions. Espinheira santa has a much longer a... - Posologie & Modes d'Administration :  - Dosage Standard : reduces acid relieves pain Leaves prevents ulcers relieves inflammation Decoction: 1 cup 2-3 times daily aids digestion cleanses blood Capsules: 1-2 g 2-3 times daily kills cancer cells increases urination kills leukemia cells mildly laxative inhibits tumors kills germs kills viruses modulates immune system prevents osteoarthritis relieves oxidative stress  - Infusion / Décoction : 1 cuillère à café à soupe de plante séchée par tasse d'eau chaude, infuser 10-15 min.  - Teinture : 2 à 4 ml (environ 30 à 60 gouttes) 2 fois par jour. - Contre-indications & Précautions :  - Consulter un professionnel de santé en cas de grossesse, allaitement ou traitement médical lourd. - Note Vitaliste : Fiche botanique officielle Rain-Tree issue des recherches du Dr. Leslie Taylor sur la pharmacopée amazonienne.  ---"
