    "fullText": "58. Genipap ( Genipa americana ) — - Famille Botanique :  - Noms Usuels / Synonymes : Genipap - Parties Utilisées : Fruit, bark, root - Catégorie Thérapeutique & Tropisme : Reins & Émonctoires (Drainage Rénal & Lithiases) - Source Primaire Rain-Tree : [Genipap Monograph on Rain-Tree.com](https://www.rain-tree.com/genipap.htm) - Principes Phytochimiques Actifs :  - carbohydrates  - sugar  - and malic acid  - Additionally  - 100 grams of the fruit provides 40 mg of calcium  - 58 mg of phosphorus and 33 mg of Vitamin C  - The fruit seeds contain 22  - 500 ppm caffeine - Indications & Cibles Thérapeutiques :  - In Guyana  - the ripe fruit is used mainly as fish bait  - The fallen  - then blue-black  - and finally jet black  - and to dye clothing - Mécanismes & Pharmacodynamie (Leslie Taylor) : 1. Actions Principales (Rain-Tree) : Documenté par Leslie Taylor pour ses principes phytochimiques actifs. 2. Recherche Clinique & Activité Biologique : Because the fruit and its infusion have unusually good keeping quality, Puerto Rican scientists investigated the possible presence of antibiotic principles and proved the existence of antibiotic activity in all parts of the fruit. In 1964, Dr. W.H. Tallent of G.D. Searle & Company in Chicago, isolated and identified 2 new antibiotic cyclopentoid monoterpenes, primarily genipic acid and secondarily... 3. Usage Ethnobotanique Traditionnel : In Guyana, the ripe fruit is used mainly as fish bait. The fallen, astringent fruits are much eaten by wild and domestic animals. The juice of the unripe fruit is colorless but oxidizes on exposure to the air and gradually turns light brown, then blue-black, and finally jet black. It has been commonly employed by South American Indians to paint the... - Posologie & Modes d'Administration :  - Dosage Standard : is nutritious repels insects fruit or juice fights free radicals increase urination 1 cup daily aids digestion kills bacteria expels worms  - Infusion / Décoction : 1 cuillère à café à soupe de plante séchée par tasse d'eau chaude, infuser 10-15 min.  - Teinture : 2 à 4 ml (environ 30 à 60 gouttes) 2 fois par jour. - Contre-indications & Précautions :  - Consulter un professionnel de santé en cas de grossesse, allaitement ou traitement médical lourd. - Note Vitaliste : Fiche botanique officielle Rain-Tree issue des recherches du Dr. Leslie Taylor sur la pharmacopée amazonienne.  ---"
