    "fullText": "64. Guandu ( Cajanus cajan ) — - Famille Botanique : Fabaceae - Noms Usuels / Synonymes : Guandu - Parties Utilisées : Leaf, flower, bean/seed - Catégorie Thérapeutique & Tropisme : Reins & Émonctoires (Drainage Rénal & Lithiases) - Source Primaire Rain-Tree : [Guandu Monograph on Rain-Tree.com](https://www.rain-tree.com/guandu.htm) - Principes Phytochimiques Actifs :  - Chemical analysis reveals guandu contains: 2'-0'methylcajanone  - 2'-hydroxygenistein  - 2'-trihydroxyisoflavone  - alpha-amyrin  - beta-amryin  - beta-sitosterol  - cajaflavanone  - cajaisoflavone - Indications & Cibles Thérapeutiques :  - In Peru  - guandu is called caja or puspo-poroto  - There the leaves are prepared in a infusion for anemia  - hepatitis  - diabetes  - urinary infections - Mécanismes & Pharmacodynamie (Leslie Taylor) : 1. Actions Principales (Rain-Tree) : Documenté par Leslie Taylor pour ses principes phytochimiques actifs. 2. Recherche Clinique & Activité Biologique : In several clinical studies scientists have reported that seed extracts of guandu inhibit red blood sickling and may be beneficial for people with sickle cell anemia. Laboratory studies with animals report that the seeds have some anti-nutritional qualities and reported to contain trypsin inhibitors and chymotrypsin inhibitors which reduce or inhibit pancreatic amylase and lipase.... 3. Usage Ethnobotanique Traditionnel : In Peru, guandu is called caja or puspo-poroto . There the leaves are prepared in a infusion for anemia, hepatitis, diabetes, urinary infections, and yellow fever. The flowers are prepared in an infusion for dysentery, and menstrual disorders; and the seeds are infused to use as a diuretic. In Brazilian herbal medicine, the leaves are infused for c... - Posologie & Modes d'Administration :  - Dosage Standard : reduces fever stops bleeding Leaves, flowers, seeds heals wounds reduces fever Infusion: 1 cup twice daily is astringent reduces mucus balances menstruation relieves coughs reduces inflammation increases urination reduces sickling  - Infusion / Décoction : 1 cuillère à café à soupe de plante séchée par tasse d'eau chaude, infuser 10-15 min.  - Teinture : 2 à 4 ml (environ 30 à 60 gouttes) 2 fois par jour. - Contre-indications & Précautions :  - Consulter un professionnel de santé en cas de grossesse, allaitement ou traitement médical lourd. - Note Vitaliste : Fiche botanique officielle Rain-Tree issue des recherches du Dr. Leslie Taylor sur la pharmacopée amazonienne.  ---"
