    "fullText": "74. Jabuticaba ( Plinia cauliflora ) — - Famille Botanique : Fabaceae - Noms Usuels / Synonymes : Jabuticaba - Parties Utilisées : Feuilles, écorce, racines ou plante entière - Catégorie Thérapeutique & Tropisme : Reins & Émonctoires (Drainage Rénal & Lithiases) - Source Primaire Rain-Tree : [Jabuticaba Monograph on Rain-Tree.com](https://www.rain-tree.com/jabuticaba.htm) - Principes Phytochimiques Actifs :  - purple and black fruits  - This group of chemicals have been shown to prevent cardiovascular disease  - and has antioxidant  - anti-diabetic  - anti-cancer  - cancer prevention  - anti-inflammatory  - antimicrobial and anti-obesity effects - Indications & Cibles Thérapeutiques :  - In Brazilian traditional medicine systems  - the fruit  - leaves and bark are used to prepare natural remedies  - These are consumed for asthma  - diarrhea  - earaches - Mécanismes & Pharmacodynamie (Leslie Taylor) : 1. Actions Principales (Rain-Tree) : Documenté par Leslie Taylor pour ses principes phytochimiques actifs. 2. Recherche Clinique & Activité Biologique : A single-blind, parallel, randomized, placebo-controlled clinical trial involving 49 individuals with Metabolic Syndrome (similar to pre-diabetes) was conducted in 2024 at the University of Campinas in Brazil. One half of the participants received 15 grams daily of a jabuticaba peel powder for 5 days and data was collected after they ate a meal. Researchers reported: “JP [jabuticaba peel] suppleme... 3. Usage Ethnobotanique Traditionnel : Jabuticaba is native to the Tupi and Guarani Indigenous Peoples lands. The fruit is a staple in their cultures as well as native Brazilians in the Amazon, with low-income families collecting and selling jaboticaba fruit to supplement their income. In Brazilian traditional medicine systems, the fruit, leaves and bark are used to prepare natural reme... - Posologie & Modes d'Administration :  - Dosage Standard : ‎fights free radicals lowers uric acid Fruit relieves oxidative stress prevents mutations Fresh Juice: 1 cup 2-3 times daily reduces inflammation balances cholesterol Capsules: 2-4 g twice daily or protects organs lowers blood sugar follow label directions on promotes weight loss lowers blood pressure kills bacteria kills cancer cells slows aging kills fungi reduces stress & anxiety prevents chronic diseases  - Infusion / Décoction : 1 cuillère à café à soupe de plante séchée par tasse d'eau chaude, infuser 10-15 min.  - Teinture : 2 à 4 ml (environ 30 à 60 gouttes) 2 fois par jour. - Contre-indications & Précautions :  - Jabuticaba may lower blood pressure and blood sugar levels. These effects were recorded in both humans and animals with effects recorded as milder in humans than in animals. Diabetics, and people with hypogylcemia and those taking hypotensive drugs should use with caution while monitoring their glucose or blood pressure levels accordingly. - Note Vitaliste : Fiche botanique officielle Rain-Tree issue des recherches du Dr. Leslie Taylor sur la pharmacopée amazonienne.  ---"
