    "fullText": "81. Maca ( Lepidium meyenii ) — - Famille Botanique :  - Noms Usuels / Synonymes : Maca - Parties Utilisées : Root - Catégorie Thérapeutique & Tropisme : Immunité & Anti-infectieux (Immunomodulateur & Antiviral) - Source Primaire Rain-Tree : [Maca Monograph on Rain-Tree.com](https://www.rain-tree.com/maca.htm) - Principes Phytochimiques Actifs :  - The nutritional value of dried maca root is high  - resembling those of cereal grains such as maize  - rice  - and wheat  - It contains 60-75% carbohydrates  - 10-14% protein  - 5% fiber  - and 2 - Indications & Cibles Thérapeutiques :  - To the Andean Indians and indigenous peoples  - maca is a valuable commodity  - Because so little else grows in the region  - corn  - green vegetables  - and beans - Mécanismes & Pharmacodynamie (Leslie Taylor) : 1. Actions Principales (Rain-Tree) : Documenté par Leslie Taylor pour ses principes phytochimiques actifs. 2. Recherche Clinique & Activité Biologique : Maca's fertility-enhancing properties were reported as early as 1961, when researchers discovered that it increased fertility in rats. Marketing and resulting sales of maca for sexual function has been fueled by clinical research since. The majority of this research, however, has been performed or funded by two main marketers of maca products in the U.S. and abroad! Also suspect to the independent... 3. Usage Ethnobotanique Traditionnel : To the Andean Indians and indigenous peoples, maca is a valuable commodity. Because so little else grows in the region, maca is often traded with communities at lower elevations for such other staples as rice, corn, green vegetables, and beans. The dried roots can be stored for up to seven years. Native Peruvians traditionally have utilized maca si... - Posologie & Modes d'Administration :  - Dosage Standard : is nutritious increases fertility Root increases energy Powder: 1 tablespoon balances body systems Capsules: 5 g twice daily  - Infusion / Décoction : 1 cuillère à café à soupe de plante séchée par tasse d'eau chaude, infuser 10-15 min.  - Teinture : 2 à 4 ml (environ 30 à 60 gouttes) 2 fois par jour. - Contre-indications & Précautions :  - None reported. - Note Vitaliste : Fiche botanique officielle Rain-Tree issue des recherches du Dr. Leslie Taylor sur la pharmacopée amazonienne.  ---"
