    "fullText": "95. Passion Fruit ( Passiflora incarnata (fruit) ) — - Famille Botanique : Passifloraceae - Noms Usuels / Synonymes : Maracuja, passionflower, passion flower, carkifelek, charkhi felek, maypop, maypop passionflower, saa't gulu, ward assa'ah, zahril aalaam, granadilla, passionvine, maracoc, apricot-vine, saa't gulu, ward assa'ah, zahril aalaam - Parties Utilisées : Vine, Leaves, Stem - Catégorie Thérapeutique & Tropisme : Reins & Émonctoires (Drainage Rénal & Lithiases) - Source Primaire Rain-Tree : [Passion Fruit Monograph on Rain-Tree.com](https://www.rain-tree.com/passionf.htm) - Principes Phytochimiques Actifs :  - These include flavonoids and their metabolites  - anthocyanins and their metabolites  - procyanidins  - and stilbenes  - Piceatannol is a stilbene polyphenol found in foods like grapes  - passion fruit  - and blueberries  - Passion fruit - Indications & Cibles Thérapeutiques :  - sleep aid  - or calming tonic  - Daniel B  - called maracuja grande  - that is frequently used to treat asthma  - whooping cough - Mécanismes & Pharmacodynamie (Leslie Taylor) : 1. Actions Principales (Rain-Tree) : Documenté par Leslie Taylor pour ses principes phytochimiques actifs. 2. Recherche Clinique & Activité Biologique : There is a significant body of research (with tens of thousands of studies) how polyphenol antioxidant chemicals, like those found in passion fruit, can treat and prevent many diseases and conditions. The research on passion fruit demonstrates the same benefits for the same conditions as described in the polyphenol research. The research published by many researchers around the world report that p... 3. Usage Ethnobotanique Traditionnel : Passion fruit has been a food staple for the people and animals of the rainforest for eons. The leaves of many of the Passiflora species are also used by indigenous tribes as a sedative, sleep aid, or calming tonic. (See Passionflower in the Tropical Plant Database) The fruit of Passiflora edulis has been used by the Brazilian Indian tribes as a he... - Posologie & Modes d'Administration :  - Dosage Standard : blocks sugar absorption supports heart function Fruit protects heart calms coughs Fresh or juiced lowers blood pressure increases urination As desired. mild sedative enhances memory Fruit powder; 1-2 tsp 2-3 fights free radicals relieves inflammation times daily reduces oxidative stress kills bacteria balances blood sugar protects cells & organs  - Infusion / Décoction : 1 cuillère à café à soupe de plante séchée par tasse d'eau chaude, infuser 10-15 min.  - Teinture : 2 à 4 ml (environ 30 à 60 gouttes) 2 fois par jour. - Contre-indications & Précautions :  - Consulter un professionnel de santé en cas de grossesse, allaitement ou traitement médical lourd. - Note Vitaliste : Fiche botanique officielle Rain-Tree issue des recherches du Dr. Leslie Taylor sur la pharmacopée amazonienne.  ---"
