    "fullText": "97. Pau d'Arco ( Tabebuia impetiginosa ) — - Famille Botanique :  - Noms Usuels / Synonymes : Pau d'Arco - Parties Utilisées : Bark, wood - Catégorie Thérapeutique & Tropisme : Reins & Émonctoires (Drainage Rénal & Lithiases) - Source Primaire Rain-Tree : [Pau d'Arco Monograph on Rain-Tree.com](https://www.rain-tree.com/paudarco.htm) - Principes Phytochimiques Actifs :  - The plant contains a large amount of chemicals known as quinoids  - and a small quantity of benzenoids and flavonoids  - These quinoids (and  - chiefly  - anthraquinones  - furanonaphthoquinones  - lapachones  - In the 1960s - Indications & Cibles Thérapeutiques :  - Throughout South America  - \" The Guarani and Tupi Indians call the tree tajy  - which means \"to have strength and vigor  - anemia  - colitis  - respiratory problems - Mécanismes & Pharmacodynamie (Leslie Taylor) : 1. Actions Principales (Rain-Tree) : Documenté par Leslie Taylor pour ses principes phytochimiques actifs. 2. Recherche Clinique & Activité Biologique : Over many years pau d’arco has continued to demonstrate anti-tumorous, anti-cancer and anti-leukemic actions in many types of cancer at low dosages without toxicity to healthy cells. These included breast carcinoma, lung carcinoma, cervical carcinoma, and liver carcinomas with the GI50 values (corresponding to a sample concentration achieving 50% growth inhibition in human tumor cell lines) report... 3. Usage Ethnobotanique Traditionnel : Pau d'arco has a long and well-documented history of use by the indigenous peoples of the rainforest. Indications imply that its use may actually predate the Incas. Throughout South America, tribes living thousands of miles apart have employed it for the same medicinal purposes for hundreds of years. Several Indian tribes of the rainforest have use... - Posologie & Modes d'Administration :  - Dosage Standard : kills bacteria prevents ulcers Bark, Heartwood kills fungi enhances immunity Decoction: 1/2 cup 2-4 kills viruses calms skin rashes times daily kills cancer cells relieves arthritis Tincture: 2-3 ml 2-3 reduces tumors protects brain times daily reduces inflammation neutralizes venom Capsules: Not recommended kills parasites protects cells relieves pain heals wounds fights free radicals modulates immune system relieves oxidative stress  - Infusion / Décoction : 1 cuillère à café à soupe de plante séchée par tasse d'eau chaude, infuser 10-15 min.  - Teinture : 2 à 4 ml (environ 30 à 60 gouttes) 2 fois par jour. - Contre-indications & Précautions :  - Consulter un professionnel de santé en cas de grossesse, allaitement ou traitement médical lourd. - Note Vitaliste : Fiche botanique officielle Rain-Tree issue des recherches du Dr. Leslie Taylor sur la pharmacopée amazonienne.  ---"
