    "fullText": "98. Pedra Hume Caa ( Myrcia salicifolia ) — - Famille Botanique :  - Noms Usuels / Synonymes : Pedra hume ca&aacute, pedra-ume-ca&aacute, insulina vegetal - Parties Utilisées : Leaves - Catégorie Thérapeutique & Tropisme : Reins & Émonctoires (Drainage Rénal & Lithiases) - Source Primaire Rain-Tree : [Pedra Hume Caa Monograph on Rain-Tree.com](https://www.rain-tree.com/pedra.htm) - Principes Phytochimiques Actifs :  - Phytochemical analysis of pedra hume caá reveals a high content of flavonoids  - flavonols  - and flavanones  - In 1998  - These new flavanone glucosides were named myrciacitrins I and II  - the new acetophenone glucosides were named myrciaphenones A and B  - and thus protect the nerves  - For this reason - Indications & Cibles Thérapeutiques :  - It is contraindicated in those with hypoglycemia - Mécanismes & Pharmacodynamie (Leslie Taylor) : 1. Actions Principales (Rain-Tree) : 1. Pedra hume caá has been documented to lower blood sugar levels in animal and human studies. It is contraindicated in those with hypoglycemia. Diabetics who wish to use this plant should seek the advice and supervision of a qualified health care practitioner while using this plant, as blood sugar levels will need to be monitored carefully and medications may need adjustments. 2. Pedra hume caá has been used in South American herbal medicine for hypertension. This use has not been substantiated or confirmed by clinical research. Those with low blood pressure and/or those on medications to lower their blood pressure should use this plant with caution and closely monitor these possible effects. 2. Recherche Clinique & Activité Biologique : Brazilian scientists have documented leaf extracts of pedra hume caá with hypoglycemic activity since 1929. Two clinical studies published in the 1990s again demonstrated its hypoglycemic activity and confirmed its traditional use for diabetes. In a 1990 double-blind placebo clinical study with normal and Type II diabetic patients, pedra hume caá (3 g powdered leaf daily) demonstrated the ability ... 3. Usage Ethnobotanique Traditionnel : Pedra hume ca&aacute; has been used by indigenous tribes in the rainforest for diabetes, diarrhea, and dysentery. The Taiwanos tribe (in northwest Amazonia) considers the leaves to be astringent and use it for persistent diarrhea. It has had a place in Brazilian traditional medicine for many years. Dr. G. L. Cruz, a leading Brazilian practitioner a... - Posologie & Modes d'Administration :  - Dosage Standard : lowers blood sugar fights free radicals Leaves improves diabetes dries secretions Infusion: 1 cup 2-3 times increases urination daily with meals protects nerves Capsules: 1-2 g 2-3 times daily with meals  - Infusion / Décoction : 1 cuillère à café à soupe de plante séchée par tasse d'eau chaude, infuser 10-15 min.  - Teinture : 2 à 4 ml (environ 30 à 60 gouttes) 2 fois par jour. - Contre-indications & Précautions :  - 1. Pedra hume caá has been documented to lower blood sugar levels in animal and human studies. It is contraindicated in those with hypoglycemia. Diabetics who wish to use this plant should seek the advice and supervision of a qualified health care practitioner while using this plant, as blood sugar levels will need to be monitored carefully and medications may need adjustments. 2. Pedra hume caá has been used in South American herbal medicine for hypertension. This use has not been substantiated or confirmed by clinical research. Those with low blood pressure and/or those on medications to lower their blood pressure should use this plant with caution and closely monitor these possible effects. - Note Vitaliste : Fiche botanique officielle Rain-Tree issue des recherches du Dr. Leslie Taylor sur la pharmacopée amazonienne.  ---"
