    "fullText": "110. Sarsaparilla ( Smilax officinalis ) — - Famille Botanique : Smilacaceae - Noms Usuels / Synonymes : Sarsaparilla, salsaparrilha, khao yen, saparna, smilace, smilax, zarzaparilla, jupicanga - Parties Utilisées : Root - Catégorie Thérapeutique & Tropisme : Reins & Émonctoires (Drainage Rénal & Lithiases) - Source Primaire Rain-Tree : [Sarsaparilla Monograph on Rain-Tree.com](https://www.rain-tree.com/sarsaparilla.htm) - Principes Phytochimiques Actifs :  - Sarsaparilla contains the plant steroids sarsasapogenin  - smilagenin  - sitosterol  - stigmasterol  - and pollinastanol  - and the saponins sarsasaponin  - smilasaponin  - sarsaparilloside - Indications & Cibles Thérapeutiques :  - rheumatism  - skin ailments  - and as a general tonic for physical weakness  - and against the common cold  - armadillos are \"on the menu\" in indigenous diets)  - European physicians considered sarsaparilla root a tonic - Mécanismes & Pharmacodynamie (Leslie Taylor) : 1. Actions Principales (Rain-Tree) : Documenté par Leslie Taylor pour ses principes phytochimiques actifs. 2. Recherche Clinique & Activité Biologique : Clinical research has validated the traditional use of sarsaparilla for skin conditions such as psoriasis, eczema, acne, and leprosy. In 1942, it was reported in the New England Journal of Medicine to improve the condition of psoriasis dramatically. There the results of a clinical study with 92 patients was detailed which reported that it improved psoriasis lesions in 62% of cases and completely c... 3. Usage Ethnobotanique Traditionnel : Sarsaparilla root has been used for centuries by the indigenous peoples of Central and South America for sexual impotence, rheumatism, skin ailments, and as a general tonic for physical weakness. It has long been used by tribes in Peru and Honduras for headaches and joint pain, and against the common cold. Many shamans and medicine men in the Amazo... - Posologie & Modes d'Administration :  - Dosage Standard : relieves psoriasis relieves pain Root fights free radicals kills fungi & bacteria Decoction: 1/2 to 1 cup 2-3 relieves oxidative stress kills viruses times daily protects organs kills parasites Capsules: 1-2 g twice daily promotes weight loss reduces fever Tincture: 2-3 ml twice daily relieves inflammation detoxifies slows aging kills cancer cells enhances memory reduces allergies prevents chronic diseases prevents gout balances immune function eases arthritis reduces depression  - Infusion / Décoction : 1 cuillère à café à soupe de plante séchée par tasse d'eau chaude, infuser 10-15 min.  - Teinture : 2 à 4 ml (environ 30 à 60 gouttes) 2 fois par jour. - Contre-indications & Précautions :  - Consulter un professionnel de santé en cas de grossesse, allaitement ou traitement médical lourd. - Note Vitaliste : Fiche botanique officielle Rain-Tree issue des recherches du Dr. Leslie Taylor sur la pharmacopée amazonienne.  ---"
