    "fullText": "120. Velvet Bean ( Mucuna pruriens ) — - Famille Botanique : Fabaceae - Noms Usuels / Synonymes : Velvet Bean - Parties Utilisées : Feuilles, écorce, racines ou plante entière - Catégorie Thérapeutique & Tropisme : Reins & Émonctoires (Drainage Rénal & Lithiases) - Source Primaire Rain-Tree : [Velvet Bean Monograph on Rain-Tree.com](https://www.rain-tree.com/velvetbean.htm) - Principes Phytochimiques Actifs :  - The seeds of velvet bean are high in protein  - carbohydrates  - lipids  - fiber  - and minerals  - They are also rich in novel alkaloids  - saponins  - and sterols - Indications & Cibles Thérapeutiques :  - It should not be used during pregnancy  - Velvet bean has shown to lower blood sugar  - Velvet bean is contraindicated in combination with M  - inhibitors  - Velvet bean has androgenic activity  - increasing testosterone levels  - Velvet bean inhibits prolactin  - The seed contains high quantities of L-dopa - Mécanismes & Pharmacodynamie (Leslie Taylor) : 1. Actions Principales (Rain-Tree) : 1. The seed may cause birth defects and has uterine stimulant activity. It should not be used during pregnancy. 2. Velvet bean has shown to lower blood sugar. Those with hypoglycemia or diabetes should only use Velvet bean under the supervision of a qualified healthcare practitioner. 3. Velvet bean is contraindicated in combination with M.A.O. inhibitors. 4. Velvet bean has androgenic activity, increasing testosterone levels. Persons with excessive androgen syndromes should avoid using Velvet bean. 5. Velvet bean inhibits prolactin. If you have a medical condition resulting in inadequate levels of prolactin in the body, do not use Velvet bean unless under the direction or your healthcare practitioner. 6. The seed contains high quantities of L-dopa. Levodopa is the pharmaceutical medication used for Parkinson's disease. Those with Parkinson's should only use velvet bean under the supervision of a qualified healthcare practitioner. 2. Recherche Clinique & Activité Biologique : Velvet bean has demonstrated little toxicity; however, it has been documented in animal studies to cause birth defects and should not be used during pregnancy. Traditionally, velvet bean has been used as a nerve tonic for nervous system disorders. Due to the high concentration of L-dopa in the seeds, it has been studied for its possible use in Parkinson's disease. Parkinson's disease is a common a... 3. Usage Ethnobotanique Traditionnel : In Central America, velvet beans have been roasted and ground to make a coffee substitute for decades; its goes by the common name of \"nescafé\" in these regions, as well as in Brazil, for this reason. It is still grown as a food crop by the Ketchi indigenous people in Guatemala; the bean is cooked as a vegetable. In Brazil the seed has been used in... - Posologie & Modes d'Administration :  - Dosage Standard : is L-Dopa alternative relieves pain Seed increases testosterone reduces inflammation Decoction: 1/2 to 1 cup increases libido kills parasites twice daily reduces spasms calms nerves Capsules: 1-2 g twice daily lowers blood sugar reduces fever Standardized extracts: lowers blood pressure lowers cholesterol Follow label instructions increases urination  - Infusion / Décoction : 1 cuillère à café à soupe de plante séchée par tasse d'eau chaude, infuser 10-15 min.  - Teinture : 2 à 4 ml (environ 30 à 60 gouttes) 2 fois par jour. - Contre-indications & Précautions :  - Consulter un professionnel de santé en cas de grossesse, allaitement ou traitement médical lourd. - Note Vitaliste : Fiche botanique officielle Rain-Tree issue des recherches du Dr. Leslie Taylor sur la pharmacopée amazonienne.  ---"
