    "fullText": "123. Sangre de Grado ( Croton lechleri ) — - Famille Botanique :  - Noms Usuels / Synonymes : Sangre de grado, sangre de drago, dragon& 8217, s blood, drago, sangue de drago, sangue de agua - Parties Utilisées : Bark, resin/sap - Catégorie Thérapeutique & Tropisme : Foie & Digestion (Hépato-Biliaire & Détox) - Source Primaire Rain-Tree : [Sangre de Grado Monograph on Rain-Tree.com](https://www.rain-tree.com/sangre.htm) - Principes Phytochimiques Actifs :  - simple phenols  - diterpenes  - phytosterols  - and a lignan named dimethylcedrusine  - Of course  - botanists  - herbalists  - in this particular case - Indications & Cibles Thérapeutiques :  - The earliest written reference dates its use to the 1600s  - when Spanish naturalist and explorer P  - Peru  - and Ecuador  - For centuries  - the sap has been painted on wounds to staunch bleeding - Mécanismes & Pharmacodynamie (Leslie Taylor) : 1. Actions Principales (Rain-Tree) : Documenté par Leslie Taylor pour ses principes phytochimiques actifs. 2. Recherche Clinique & Activité Biologique : The wound-healing action of sangre de grado resin was first related to the taspine alkaloid in 1989. Several later studies also concentrated on the wound-healing and antitumorous properties of taspine. The lignan dimethylcedrusine was isolated by scientists in 1993 and was shown to play a central role in sangre de grado's effective wound-healing action. This Belgian study revealed that the crude r... 3. Usage Ethnobotanique Traditionnel : Sangre de grado's red sap or latex (and also its bark) has a long history of indigenous use in the rainforest and in South America. The earliest written reference dates its use to the 1600s, when Spanish naturalist and explorer P. Bernabé Cobo found that the curative power of the sap was widely known throughout the indigenous tribes of Mexico, Peru... - Posologie & Modes d'Administration :  - Dosage Standard : heals wounds kills cancer cells Resin stops bleeding prevents tumor growth Internal: 10 to 15 drops kills bacteria stops mutations twice daily kills germs External: Apply to affected kills fungi area twice daily kills viruses relieves diarrhea reduces inflammation relieves itching  - Infusion / Décoction : 1 cuillère à café à soupe de plante séchée par tasse d'eau chaude, infuser 10-15 min.  - Teinture : 2 à 4 ml (environ 30 à 60 gouttes) 2 fois par jour. - Contre-indications & Précautions :  - None reported. - Note Vitaliste : Fiche botanique officielle Rain-Tree issue des recherches du Dr. Leslie Taylor sur la pharmacopée amazonienne.  ---"
