    "excerpt": "- Famille Botanique :  - Noms Usuels / Synonymes : Muira puama - Parties Utilisées : Bark and root - Catégorie Thérapeutique & Tropisme : Antiparasitaire & Antifongique (Purification & Antiparasitaire) - Source Primaire Rain-Tree : [Muira puama Monograph on Rain-Tree.com](https://www.rain-tree.com/muirapuama.htm) - Pri...",
    "fullText": "125. Muira puama ( Ptychopetalum olacoides ) — - Famille Botanique :  - Noms Usuels / Synonymes : Muira puama - Parties Utilisées : Bark and root - Catégorie Thérapeutique & Tropisme : Antiparasitaire & Antifongique (Purification & Antiparasitaire) - Source Primaire Rain-Tree : [Muira puama Monograph on Rain-Tree.com](https://www.rain-tree.com/muirapuama.htm) - Principes Phytochimiques Actifs :  - essential oils (including beta-caryophyllene and alpha-humulene)  - plant sterols  - triterpenes (including lupeol)  - and a new alkaloid-which they named muirapuamine  - sesquiterpenes  - monoterpenes  - and novel alkaloids  - The main plant chemicals found in muira puama include: 6α - Indications & Cibles Thérapeutiques :  - Historically  - all parts of muira puama have been used medicinally  - and a root-and-bark tea is taken to treat sexual debility  - rheumatism  - grippe  - and cardiac and gastrointestinal weakness - Mécanismes & Pharmacodynamie (Leslie Taylor) : 1. Actions Principales (Rain-Tree) : Documenté par Leslie Taylor pour ses principes phytochimiques actifs. 2. Recherche Clinique & Activité Biologique : In one of the early studies, researchers indicated that muira puama was effective in treating disorders of the nervous system and sexual impotence, and that \"permanent effect is produced in locomotor ataxia, neuralgias of long standing, chronic rheumatism, and partial paralysis.\" In 1930, Meiro Penna wrote about muira puama in his book Notas Sobre Plantas Brasilerias. He cited physiological and th... 3. Usage Ethnobotanique Traditionnel : Historically, all parts of muira puama have been used medicinally, but the bark and roots are the most-utilized parts of the plant. It has long been used in the Amazon by indigenous peoples for a number of purposes. Native peoples along the Brazilian Amazon's Rio Negro river use the stems and roots from young plants as a tonic to treat neuromuscula... - Posologie & Modes d'Administration :  - Dosage Standard : increase libido is a male tonic Root, bark promotes sexual function relieves pain Tincture: 2-4 ml twice daily calms nerves reduces fatigue Decoction: 1 cup daily relieves depression lowers blood pressure enhances memory prevents ulcers protects brain cells  - Infusion / Décoction : 1 cuillère à café à soupe de plante séchée par tasse d'eau chaude, infuser 10-15 min.  - Teinture : 2 à 4 ml (environ 30 à 60 gouttes) 2 fois par jour. - Contre-indications & Précautions :  - None reported. - Note Vitaliste : Fiche botanique officielle Rain-Tree issue des recherches du Dr. Leslie Taylor sur la pharmacopée amazonienne.  ---"
